    "q-97034": {
      "dom_id": "step-q97034",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Let\n$T=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nbe the standard matrix of the linear transformation $T.$ Then $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that $T$ has proportional rows, and yet $T$ is not the zero matrix. \n\nTherefore, $\\text{rank}(T)=1$ and $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto a line that passes through the origin.\n\nMoreover, the line must pass through the origin $(0,0)$ and the points $(1,-1)$ and $(-1,1),$ which are defined by the columns of the matrix $T.$ \n\nComputing the slope $m$ of this line, we get\n\n$$\nm=\\frac{1-(-1)}{-1-1}=-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto the line $y=-x.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-97034-a",
