    "q-97068": {
      "dom_id": "step-q97068",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Let\n$T=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{aligned}]$\nbe the standard matrix of the linear transformation $T.$ Then $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that $T$ has proportional rows, and yet $T$ is not the zero matrix. \n\nTherefore, $\\text{rank}(T)=1$ and $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto a line that passes through the origin.\n\nMoreover, the line must pass through the origin $(0,0)$ and the points $(1,4)$ and $(2,8),$ which are defined by the columns of the matrix $T.$ \n\nComputing the slope $m$ of this line, we get\n\n$$\nm=\\frac{8-4}{2-1}=4.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto the line $y=4x.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
